/-!
# The infinitesimal neighbourhoods of a zero scheme on the standard opens of a section ring

Let `X` be a scheme, `L` an ample invertible `𝒪_X`-module, `s ∈ Γ(X, L)` with zero scheme
`Q = Z(s)`, and `ℱ` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module with graded module `M = Γ_*(X, L, ℱ)` over the
section ring `A = Γ_*(X, L)`; write `f ∈ A₁` for `s`. Let `β ∈ Γ(X, L ^⊗ e)` be a homogeneous
element of positive degree `e` with affine nonvanishing open `W = X_β`.

This file describes the restriction of `ℱ` to the infinitesimal neighbourhood `Q_{e k}` over `W`
in terms of the localization `M_β`: a section `y ∈ Γ(W, ℱ)` dies on `Q_{e k}` exactly when its
image in `M_β` — the degree-zero element of Stacks Tag 01PW — is `f^{e k}` times an element of
degree `-e k`. The two inputs are

* the ideal of `Q_{e k}` on `W`: it is generated by the `k`-th power of the function `c` with
  `sᵉ|_W = c · β|_W`, because `Q_e = Z(sᵉ)`
  (`Stacks.Algebraization.zeroScheme_powSec_degreeOneSection`) and `β` generates `L ^⊗ e` on `W`;
* the semilinearity of the division of Tag 01PW over the chart ring map, which carries the
  function `c` to the degree-zero fraction `fᵉ / β`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SectionRingChartTower.exists_smul_mk_iff`: in the localization `M_β`, the multiples of
  `f^{e m}` by elements of degree `-e m` are the multiples of `(fᵉ/β)ᵐ` by elements of degree
  zero.
* `Stacks.SectionRingChartTower.unit_app_surjective` and `mem_ker_unit_app_iff`: the restriction
  to a closed subscheme with ideal `Iⁿ`, on the sections over an affine open.
* `Stacks.SectionRingChartTower.zeroScheme_pow_ideal_chart`: the ideal of `Q_{e k}` on `X_β`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EL1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EL1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01PW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01PW)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

